# The part with the executable forms and the argument of the receiver fn of that name are called `code` (the author
# 2026-11-11, the book, data-code-roles): the former spelling `body` names no formal of the receiver's contract, so the
# written arguments bind no form of it -- answer 5 where the root reaches the declaration.
fn: name := k1; args := (int: a); return := int; body := (return: a + 1)
int: r k1(2)
